    {
      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.62,
      "end": 1.7,
      "text": "Hey, how are you doing?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.69,
      "end": 16.24,
      "text": "That's the plastic lens oxidising from the sun. It also makes the lights dimmer, so it's worth fixing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.7,
      "end": 26.67,
      "text": "Usually not. A headlight restoration kit sands the cloudy layer off and polishes it clear, then adds a protective coating."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 30.72,
      "end": 37.17,
      "text": "Toothpaste can help a little for light haze, but it doesn't last. A proper kit with a UV sealant stays clear for a year or more."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 39.99,
      "end": 46.33,
      "text": "Not really. Mask off the paint around the light with tape, take your time with each sanding step, and do it on a dry day."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 49.94,
      "end": 53.65,
      "text": "Nice. You'll be surprised how much brighter the road looks afterwards."
    }
  ]
